# Lazav, Wearer of Faces (turn 3): attacking, it exiles the Ornithopter from Bot1's graveyard (a creature card, a 0/2 flyer) and
# investigates (CR 701.16a). In the second main phase Bot1 sacrifices that Clue, and Lazav's second ability lets it become a copy
# of the exiled Ornithopter (CR 707.2): Lazav's name and 2/3 are replaced by the Ornithopter's 0/2 with flying, and the Clue's
# draw still happens. Lazav stays the same object (CR 707.4), so the Ornithopter stays in exile with it.
# At the end of the turn the copy effect ends (CR 514.2) and it is Lazav, Wearer of Faces again, 2/3 and damaged by nothing.

